Hard to say. With these kind of monsters, the preparation is more  
important than the actual level... A poorly leveled up character of XL20  
would die in front of a titan while a cleaverly prepared character of XL  
~12-14 can handle it without too much damage...

There is one guaranteed titan in one of the version of Medusa level and it  
seldom means good news when you found him... If I haven't done the quest  
yet, finding the titan at Medusa is usually a good motivation for going  
there...

Have good AC (say -10 or -15 at least), lots of HPs (150 ?), means of  
healing (alchemise FH), means of escape ((cursed) scrolls of teleport) or  
of delay (wand of teleport), see invisible (it can cast make invisible on  
self and maybe also on other monsters), buffed up weapons/spells, means of  
deal with the summoning storm (wand of fire/lightning/fireball, (non  
cursed) scroll of scare monster). And be prepared to use a lo of your  
gear, Titan certainly rank amongst the strongest monsters and you probably  
shouldn't met big As before hell and you can genocide Ls.

Alternatively, bring a purple worm and a ring of conflict.

